1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,628
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,712 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,478 --> 00:00:21,688
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,771 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,738
[Arnaldo] <i>I'm jealous of your close</i>

6
00:00:29,821 --> 00:00:31,990
<i>friendship with this</i>

7
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:33,408
<i>Lily Cruz.</i>

8
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:36,327
<i>I'm not talking about</i>
<i>the Lily Cruz that you're with.</i>

9
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:37,412
[Arnaldo] <i>She's an impostor.</i>

10
00:00:37,495 --> 00:00:39,539
<i>That's right.</i>

11
00:00:39,622 --> 00:00:42,250
[Arnaldo] <i>I'm going to make her regret</i>
<i>all the things that she did to me.</i>

12
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:43,418
<i>And then, I'll kill her.</i>

13
00:00:43,501 --> 00:00:44,961
[Anna] <i>What happened to Lily?</i>

14
00:00:45,044 --> 00:00:46,671
<i>-I have to go save her!</i>
<i>-There's a bomb, everyone!</i>

15
00:00:46,755 --> 00:00:49,424
-[woman] <i>There's a bomb!</i>
-[Julio laughs]

16
00:00:49,507 --> 00:00:51,259
<i>It was just planted here to scare you.</i>

17
00:00:51,342 --> 00:00:54,012
[grunting]

18
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:57,348
[Diego] <i>Lily's life is in danger.</i>

19
00:00:57,432 --> 00:00:58,933
<i>I'm coming with you, Diego.</i>

20
00:00:59,017 --> 00:01:01,144
[Diego] <i>I promise I'll bring</i>
<i>back Ivy safe and sound.</i>

21
00:01:01,227 --> 00:01:02,270
[Jepoy] <i>Diego, I'll come with you.</i>

22
00:01:02,353 --> 00:01:04,105
[Arnaldo] <i>You're Lily Cruz,</i>
<i>right? Answer me!</i>

23
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:07,317
<i>Yes! I am Lily Cruz!</i>

24
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:10,820
[Damian] <i>You need to stay there so we know</i>

25
00:01:10,904 --> 00:01:14,032
<i>Julio Ardiente's every move.</i>

26
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:18,119
<i>That's the only way</i>
<i>we can take everything from him.</i>

27
00:01:18,203 --> 00:01:19,788
[Diego] <i>Arnaldo! Put the gun down!</i>

28
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:21,998
<i>No! If I can't have her, you can't either.</i>

29
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:23,124
<i>-Arnaldo!</i>
<i>-No!</i>

30
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:24,542
-[gunshot]
-[Ivy screams]

31
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:26,377
[Ivy] <i>Get out of here.</i>
<i>I'll take care of this.</i>

32
00:01:26,461 --> 00:01:28,421
<i>-I'll bring him to the hospital.</i>
-[Jose] <i>Congressman.</i>

33
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:30,173
<i>-Something happened to the mayor.</i>
<i>-What?</i>

34
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:31,883
<i>He's in critical condition</i>
<i>at the hospital.</i>

35
00:01:37,430 --> 00:01:41,226
[tense music playing]

36
00:01:56,950 --> 00:02:03,164
[Damian] <i>I'm back, Raul.</i>
<i>Your reign as Jaguar is over.</i>

37
00:02:07,085 --> 00:02:09,462
[police siren wailing]

38
00:02:10,338 --> 00:02:11,548
[Damian] <i>Mr. Cop!</i>

39
00:02:11,631 --> 00:02:14,884
<i>Catch me if you can!</i>

40
00:02:15,426 --> 00:02:17,470
-<i>Mr. Cop!</i>
-[gunshot]

41
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:22,350
[tense music playing]

42
00:02:22,433 --> 00:02:24,769
[gunshots]

43
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:26,312
[honks]

44
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,982
[screeching]

45
00:02:31,651 --> 00:02:33,778
[police officer] <i>Get out!</i>
<i>Put down your gun!</i>

46
00:02:34,487 --> 00:02:36,030
[Damian] <i>Take it easy!</i>

47
00:02:37,782 --> 00:02:39,409
<i>Dante! Dante!</i>

48
00:02:42,203 --> 00:02:44,747
<i>I need your help.</i>

49
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:47,458
<i>Get me out of here.</i>

50
00:02:48,918 --> 00:02:52,714
<i>I've told you so many times</i>
<i>but you still haven't changed.</i>

51
00:02:53,256 --> 00:02:55,717
<i>When will you learn your lesson?</i>
<i>When you're dead?</i>

52
00:02:55,967 --> 00:02:57,302
<i>What are you so proud of?</i>

53
00:02:57,385 --> 00:03:00,179
<i>It's not like you're getting</i>
<i>anything out of being a lawyer!</i>

54
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:03,683
<i>Money isn't the reason</i>
<i>why I chose to be a lawyer.</i>

55
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:07,687
<i>I became one so I can put</i>
<i>all criminals like you in jail.</i>

56
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:11,941
<i>Brother or not, I'll have you locked up</i>

57
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:13,818
<i>if that's what it takes</i>
<i>to set you straight.</i>

58
00:03:14,402 --> 00:03:16,946
<i>Then you're a useless brother,</i>
<i>you bastard!</i>

59
00:03:21,951 --> 00:03:23,745
<i>My family and I are leaving.</i>

60
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:26,998
<i>We'll start over somewhere far away.</i>

61
00:03:32,462 --> 00:03:34,339
<i>You're abandoning me.</i>

62
00:03:35,798 --> 00:03:37,842
<i>Damian, I'm begging you.</i>

63
00:03:37,926 --> 00:03:41,429
<i>Please change. I can't help you anymore.</i>

64
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:47,602
<i>Then leave. You talk like you're all that!</i>

65
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:52,273
<i>I don't need you, Attorney Cruz.</i>
<i>I can get out of here on my own!</i>

66
00:03:52,357 --> 00:03:54,776
<i>And you can forget</i>
<i>that you have a brother!</i>

67
00:03:57,862 --> 00:03:59,239
<i>Get out!</i>

68
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:09,415
-[indistinct shouts]
-[grunting]

69
00:04:16,881 --> 00:04:19,759
[grunting]

70
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:23,054
[guards blow whistle]

71
00:04:23,137 --> 00:04:24,430
[Rufo] <i>What's going on?! Stop that!</i>

72
00:04:25,181 --> 00:04:26,307
<i>That's enough!</i>

73
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:28,226
[police officer 2] <i>Stop! Stop!</i>

74
00:04:30,019 --> 00:04:32,105
-<i>Aren't you going to stop?!</i>
-[Damian grunts]

75
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:34,857
<i>Follow me! Stand up!</i>

76
00:04:35,441 --> 00:04:36,901
[police officer 2] <i>Stubborn, eh?</i>

77
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:39,362
-<i>Take care of that!</i>
-[police officer 2] <i>Yes, sir.</i>

78
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:40,780
<i>I'll take care of him.</i>

79
00:04:41,739 --> 00:04:42,907
[reporter] <i>A prisoner escaped</i>

80
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:45,368
<i>prison after a riot</i>
<i>broke out at the City Jail.</i>

81
00:04:46,035 --> 00:04:49,622
<i>Give me the keys or I'll put</i>
<i>a hole in your head.</i>

82
00:04:49,706 --> 00:04:51,124
<i>Hand it over.</i>

83
00:04:51,207 --> 00:04:53,001
[reporter] <i>In other news,</i>
<i>a sports car was stolen</i>

84
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:55,670
<i>by unknown men in Quezon City last night.</i>

85
00:04:55,753 --> 00:04:57,380
[Damian] <i>Rufo, hurry up.</i>

86
00:04:57,463 --> 00:05:00,258
-[siren wailing in distance]
-<i>I can see the police cars.</i>

87
00:05:03,511 --> 00:05:04,887
[Damian] <i>Let's go!</i>

88
00:05:06,055 --> 00:05:08,391
<i>Drive faster, donut hogs!</i>

89
00:05:09,058 --> 00:05:12,437
-[gunshots]
-[Damian laughs]

90
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:17,567
[reporter] <i>An SUV was stolen</i>
<i>by thieves in Makati last night.</i>

91
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:19,569
[reporter] <i>According to reports,</i>

92
00:05:19,652 --> 00:05:21,404
<i>the leader of the group</i>
<i>responsible for many crimes</i>

93
00:05:21,487 --> 00:05:23,865
<i>in Metro Manila calls himself the Jaguar.</i>

94
00:05:24,198 --> 00:05:25,658
[Damian] <i>Looking good!</i>

95
00:05:30,705 --> 00:05:34,375
[Rufo] <i>Mr. Jaguar.</i>
<i>What's with our new get-up?</i>

96
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:40,048
<i>This look suits us because</i>
<i>we're in the big leagues now.</i>

97
00:05:40,131 --> 00:05:41,799
[laughs]

98
00:05:42,341 --> 00:05:49,057
<i>Stealing cars got old real fast.</i>
<i>I want us to enter…</i>

99
00:05:49,515 --> 00:05:55,855
<i>smuggling, kidnapping,</i>
<i>gambling, extortion,</i>

100
00:05:56,522 --> 00:05:59,776
<i>and illegal drugs!</i>

101
00:05:59,859 --> 00:06:02,403
<i>Are we going to go against big syndicates?</i>

102
00:06:03,196 --> 00:06:05,073
<i>We'll take them all down.</i>

103
00:06:05,656 --> 00:06:07,450
[laughs hysterically]

104
00:06:10,953 --> 00:06:13,331
[Damian sighs]

105
00:06:15,083 --> 00:06:16,542
[car screeches]

106
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:17,919
[Damian] <i>Get down!</i>

107
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:22,799
[man] <i>What's this?!</i>
<i>What's the meaning of this?!</i>

108
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:25,593
[man] <i>We didn't do anything wrong!</i>

109
00:06:26,344 --> 00:06:27,762
[Rufo] <i>Follow him!</i>

110
00:06:33,059 --> 00:06:34,936
-[screeches]
-[Rufo] <i>Hurry!</i>

111
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:40,566
-[henchman] <i>Okay.</i>
-[Damian] <i>Buboy!</i>

112
00:06:43,861 --> 00:06:44,987
[ominous music playing]

113
00:06:45,571 --> 00:06:46,781
[Rufo] <i>Put your guns down!</i>

114
00:06:46,864 --> 00:06:48,908
<i>Sir, have mercy, sir.</i>

115
00:06:48,991 --> 00:06:50,493
-<i>Rufo--</i>
-[henchman] <i>Have mercy, sir.</i>

116
00:06:50,576 --> 00:06:52,286
[Damian] <i>I feel sorry for him.</i>

117
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,039
[gunshot]

118
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:57,792
[laughs hysterically]

119
00:06:58,543 --> 00:07:00,753
<i>I thought I emptied it.</i>

120
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:03,798
[gun clinks on ground]

121
00:07:07,593 --> 00:07:09,846
[henchmen] <i>Move! Get out! Hurry up!</i>

122
00:07:10,555 --> 00:07:12,098
[Damian] <i>Take everything!</i>

123
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:19,939
[laughs hysterically]

124
00:07:21,149 --> 00:07:23,609
[gunshots]

125
00:07:27,738 --> 00:07:29,866
[laughs hysterically]

126
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:31,742
[Rufo] <i>Mr. Jaguar!</i>

127
00:07:31,826 --> 00:07:34,787
<i>The police tracked us down.</i>
<i>We need to leave this place.</i>

128
00:07:34,871 --> 00:07:37,957
[guns firing]

129
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:41,419
[Rufo] <i>Let's go!</i>

130
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:44,630
[police siren wailing in distance]

131
00:07:45,006 --> 00:07:46,174
[gunshots]

132
00:07:46,257 --> 00:07:47,842
[Rufo] <i>Hurry and get the car!</i>

133
00:07:47,925 --> 00:07:49,260
<i>Mr. Jaguar, let's get out of here!</i>

134
00:07:49,343 --> 00:07:51,345
[Damian] <i>Go! Leave!</i>

135
00:07:52,805 --> 00:07:54,974
<i>-But, sir!</i>
<i>-Take care of this. Hurry!</i>

136
00:07:55,641 --> 00:07:56,642
<i>Let's go!</i>

137
00:07:56,934 --> 00:07:58,102
[Damian] <i>Leave now!</i>

138
00:07:59,854 --> 00:08:00,897
[policeman 1] <i>Stop!</i>

139
00:08:01,606 --> 00:08:02,523
[policeman 2] <i>Put your hands up!</i>

140
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:04,233
[policeman 2] <i>Put your hands up!</i>
<i>Go and handcuff him!</i>

141
00:08:04,317 --> 00:08:05,151
<i>Sir, Ouch!</i>

142
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:06,986
<i>Ouch!</i>

143
00:08:07,069 --> 00:08:07,945
[policeman 1] <i>Where's Jaguar?</i>

144
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:10,740
<i>He went there. He ran away, sir.</i>

145
00:08:11,115 --> 00:08:14,368
-[policeman 1] <i>Get him.</i>
-<i>Carry me! Carry me! Ouch!</i>

146
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:17,538
[Rufo] <i>Boss. All our money's gone.</i>

147
00:08:18,247 --> 00:08:19,707
<i>The police took everything.</i>

148
00:08:20,166 --> 00:08:24,003
<i>Our operations have to continue</i>
<i>so we can recover our losses.</i>

149
00:08:24,337 --> 00:08:25,838
[Damian] <i>Find someone</i>

150
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:29,133
<i>who'll pretend to be</i>
<i>Jaguar while I'm here.</i>

151
00:08:29,717 --> 00:08:31,552
<i>Boss. Can't I do it?</i>

152
00:08:32,803 --> 00:08:35,181
<i>Rufo, you're still young.</i>

153
00:08:36,182 --> 00:08:37,850
<i>You can't do it yet.</i>

154
00:08:37,934 --> 00:08:40,811
<i>We need someone who has experience.</i>

155
00:08:41,562 --> 00:08:44,774
<i>Someone who has connections</i>
<i>with powerful people.</i>

156
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:49,487
<i>Someone who knows</i>
<i>how to run a syndicate too.</i>

157
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:52,657
[suspenseful music playing]

158
00:08:53,824 --> 00:08:57,328
[phone ringing]

159
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:04,001
[Damian] <i>Raul Torillo?</i>

160
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:05,878
<i>Yes. Who's this?</i>

161
00:09:05,962 --> 00:09:07,755
<i>It's Jaguar.</i>

162
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:10,508
<i>Have my people talked to you yet?</i>

163
00:09:10,925 --> 00:09:11,884
<i>Yes. Why?</i>

164
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:14,470
<i>Now you know why I called.</i>

165
00:09:14,887 --> 00:09:18,849
<i>Hold on. Let me ask you.</i>
<i>Why did you choose me?</i>

166
00:09:19,183 --> 00:09:23,187
<i>Because I want to take</i>
<i>your family's gambling den.</i>

167
00:09:23,896 --> 00:09:25,773
[Damian] <i>Word on the street is,</i>

168
00:09:26,524 --> 00:09:27,775
<i>that you don't like them.</i>

169
00:09:28,609 --> 00:09:30,736
<i>So, if you want to get even with them,</i>

170
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:33,072
<i>I will support you.</i>

171
00:09:33,698 --> 00:09:35,074
<i>You provide the money.</i>

172
00:09:35,658 --> 00:09:37,660
<i>I'll provide the people and the guns.</i>

173
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:39,745
<i>All you have to do is pretend</i>

174
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:42,039
<i>to be Jaguar while I'm in prison.</i>

175
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:45,626
<i>It'll benefit us both. It's a win-win.</i>

176
00:09:52,216 --> 00:09:58,014
[Damian] <i>Now get ready, Raul.</i>
<i>The original is back.</i>

177
00:09:58,931 --> 00:10:02,727
<i>And nothing beats the original.</i>

178
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:13,029
[Emilia] Arnaldo! Arnaldo! Doc!

179
00:10:15,072 --> 00:10:16,073
[Claire] Ivy!

180
00:10:16,157 --> 00:10:17,491
[Ivy] Arnaldo!

181
00:10:17,575 --> 00:10:19,327
-[Claire] What happened?
-[Ivy] Mamita.

182
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:23,414
Doc, where's Arnaldo?
How is our son? Please, please!

183
00:10:23,497 --> 00:10:25,291
The operation was successful.

184
00:10:25,916 --> 00:10:28,669
[doctor] We were able to extract
the bullet out of his head.

185
00:10:28,961 --> 00:10:32,089
Right now, he is in
a medically-induced coma.

186
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:35,968
And that is to give time
to his brain to heal itself.

187
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:36,802
[Claire] Coma?

188
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:38,596
[doctor] Mayor Arnaldo is very lucky

189
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:42,058
he did not incur
any vital brain tissue damage.

190
00:10:43,559 --> 00:10:44,852
Colonel.

191
00:10:44,935 --> 00:10:47,647
Ms. Aguas, come with me.

192
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:50,650
[tense music playing]

193
00:10:50,733 --> 00:10:52,276
Why? Congressman?

194
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:55,613
-[Jose] Come with me.
-No! Stop it!

195
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:00,451
Hey! That hurts!

196
00:11:01,243 --> 00:11:03,120
-Ouch!
-Stand here!

197
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:05,790
[Ivy] Ouch!

198
00:11:06,874 --> 00:11:09,043
Congressman! What's the meaning of this?!

199
00:11:10,711 --> 00:11:13,130
Tell me the truth, Ivy.

200
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:18,302
Who shot Arnaldo?!

201
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:20,596
It was a man!

202
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:24,558
A man shot Arnaldo!

203
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:27,061
I was going to help him,
but it was too late!

204
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:29,939
He shot Arnaldo and got away!

205
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:31,732
You didn't recognize him?!

206
00:11:31,816 --> 00:11:34,777
How could I when he had
a bonnet on his face?!

207
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:37,363
[tense music continues]

208
00:11:37,446 --> 00:11:39,198
-[grunts]
-You and Arnaldo

209
00:11:39,281 --> 00:11:40,658
were the only ones on that yacht.

210
00:11:40,741 --> 00:11:44,578
It was you! You were the one
who shot my grandson!

211
00:11:44,662 --> 00:11:49,333
You! You were the one
who tried to kill Arnaldo!

212
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:51,252
[tense music swells]

213
00:11:51,669 --> 00:11:52,795
[Julio groans]

214
00:11:53,504 --> 00:11:54,880
[grunting]

215
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:56,549
[Ivy] I didn't--

216
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:03,931
Go ahead.

217
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:15,860
[tense music swells]

218
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:17,528
Do it, Emilia.

219
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:23,617
If I inject this into you,
you'll be the first one to die.

220
00:12:25,202 --> 00:12:28,038
Your heart will be the first one to go.

221
00:12:30,374 --> 00:12:31,625
Do you want that?

222
00:12:35,921 --> 00:12:38,716
I'm not the one who shot Arnaldo!

223
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:42,303
Put that down. Put that down!

224
00:12:45,764 --> 00:12:47,141
I'll say it again.

225
00:12:47,224 --> 00:12:50,102
I'm not the one who shot Arnaldo!

226
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:54,732
If you don't believe me,
then go ahead! Kill me!

227
00:12:56,400 --> 00:13:02,448
I admire your bravery,
Ms. Aguas. Do you play poker?!

228
00:13:03,115 --> 00:13:07,036
Because how I'd love
to call your bluff right now!

229
00:13:07,661 --> 00:13:11,749
Colonel! Take her out of here!
Take that woman away!

230
00:13:11,832 --> 00:13:14,919
Just try and fight back! Out!

231
00:13:24,678 --> 00:13:25,930
That damned liar!

232
00:13:29,099 --> 00:13:31,685
[Camia] Diego, why did you leave Lily?!

233
00:13:31,769 --> 00:13:33,312
You put her life in danger!

234
00:13:33,395 --> 00:13:35,856
Don't you know what
the Ardientes could do to her?!

235
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,942
Auntie, we had no choice.
Lily would've been discovered--

236
00:13:38,025 --> 00:13:41,153
When Arnaldo wakes up, Lily's done for!

237
00:13:41,654 --> 00:13:43,447
The Ardientes will kill her!

238
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:45,574
What time is she supposed to call?

239
00:13:45,908 --> 00:13:47,576
[Diego] Before the night ends.

240
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:48,577
If she doesn't call,

241
00:13:48,661 --> 00:13:51,622
I'm going with you to the Ardientes.

242
00:13:52,831 --> 00:13:54,416
-[Diego] Auntie. Auntie.
-[Anna] Auntie.

243
00:14:07,179 --> 00:14:10,015
-[heart rate monitor beeping]
-[oxygen machine running]

244
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:15,646
[somber music playing]

245
00:14:25,948 --> 00:14:29,785
[beeping continues]

246
00:14:47,887 --> 00:14:50,806
What have they done to you?

247
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:57,479
You aren't going to die, Arnaldo.

248
00:14:59,231 --> 00:15:04,570
Not on my watch. You are not going to die.

249
00:15:05,946 --> 00:15:08,616
I won't be burying my own grandson.

250
00:15:12,369 --> 00:15:16,874
I'll be the one to say
when you should die.

251
00:15:18,125 --> 00:15:21,337
You don't die until I say so!

252
00:15:25,299 --> 00:15:28,260
Whoever did this will pay, Arnaldo.

253
00:15:30,679 --> 00:15:34,683
You fight… You fight for your life!

254
00:15:36,226 --> 00:15:38,812
You're not supposed to die.

255
00:15:45,152 --> 00:15:46,487
[door opens]

256
00:15:50,366 --> 00:15:53,035
[somber music continues playing]

257
00:16:39,748 --> 00:16:43,335
[tense music playing]

258
00:16:48,632 --> 00:16:50,175
[henchman] Stop resisting!

259
00:16:51,093 --> 00:16:52,094
I said, stop resisting!

260
00:16:52,636 --> 00:16:53,971
[grunting]

261
00:17:02,896 --> 00:17:04,273
[buzzing]

262
00:17:04,356 --> 00:17:06,358
[tense music swells]

263
00:17:07,818 --> 00:17:09,153
[henchman] Get her inside. Hurry!

264
00:17:13,032 --> 00:17:14,116
Let's go.

265
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:16,243
Lock the door.

266
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:23,250
<i>We're now at Ardiente Hospital</i>
<i>where Mayor Torillo</i>

267
00:17:23,333 --> 00:17:25,210
<i>is currently confined</i>

268
00:17:25,294 --> 00:17:27,004
<i>after being shot in the head</i>

269
00:17:27,087 --> 00:17:29,131
<i>by an unknown assailant.</i>

270
00:17:30,632 --> 00:17:31,925
<i>Congressman…</i>

271
00:17:32,009 --> 00:17:35,012
Can you please tell us what happened?

272
00:17:38,849 --> 00:17:41,560
<i>Someone tried to murder</i>
<i>my grandson.</i>

273
00:17:42,519 --> 00:17:43,896
[Julio on TV] <i>We don't know who.</i>

274
00:17:44,813 --> 00:17:46,607
<i>Someone tried to</i>
<i>assassinate him.</i>

275
00:17:47,775 --> 00:17:49,860
[reporter on TV] <i>So, how is he doing now?</i>

276
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:53,238
<i>He's in a coma right now.</i>

277
00:17:53,322 --> 00:17:55,449
<i>But I know my grandson.</i>
<i>He's a fighter.</i>

278
00:17:55,908 --> 00:17:57,785
<i>He won't give up that easily.</i>

279
00:17:58,452 --> 00:18:00,996
<i>The only thing I ask of</i>
<i>our people right now</i>

280
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:03,165
<i>is to please pray for</i>
<i>his speedy recovery</i>

281
00:18:03,248 --> 00:18:05,417
from his current status.

282
00:18:05,918 --> 00:18:08,462
Is it true that the mayor was
with Ms. Ivy Aguas

283
00:18:08,545 --> 00:18:10,089
<i>during the incident?</i>

284
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:11,507
<i>Yes.</i>

285
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:13,342
[reporter on TV] <i>Where is she now?</i>

286
00:18:13,425 --> 00:18:15,427
<i>May we ask her for a statement?</i>

287
00:18:16,261 --> 00:18:19,973
<i>Ivy Aguas was the sole witness</i>
<i>to that incident.</i>

288
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:25,979
<i>And that's why we've decided</i>
<i>to hide her, for her safety.</i>

289
00:18:26,355 --> 00:18:28,982
<i>Her life is already in danger.</i>

290
00:18:30,317 --> 00:18:33,570
<i>Whoever tried to murder my grandson…</i>

291
00:18:39,326 --> 00:18:42,329
<i>will most likely target Ivy next.</i>

292
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:48,710
Liar. Where is my daughter?!
Tell us where she is!

293
00:18:49,878 --> 00:18:50,796
[Jose] Congressman,

294
00:18:50,879 --> 00:18:53,173
the CCTV cameras were
turned off at that time.

295
00:18:53,882 --> 00:18:55,968
[Jose] It's possible that
Miss Aguas shot the mayor

296
00:18:56,051 --> 00:18:58,220
but it's also possible that she didn't.

297
00:18:58,303 --> 00:19:01,306
The police are conducting
an investigation, Julio.

298
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:03,142
I don't care about them.

299
00:19:03,892 --> 00:19:06,812
We'll conduct our own investigation.

300
00:19:06,895 --> 00:19:09,148
[Julio] Colonel, I don't know
how you're going to do it,

301
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:12,568
but I want you to get
a copy of the ballistics report

302
00:19:12,651 --> 00:19:15,320
of the bullet
that shot Arnaldo in the head.

303
00:19:15,863 --> 00:19:18,073
And I want you to look
for other witnesses.

304
00:19:18,615 --> 00:19:19,741
Right away, sir.

305
00:19:20,159 --> 00:19:22,452
Papa, what do we do with Ivy Aguas?

306
00:19:23,203 --> 00:19:25,247
I will interrogate her
until the truth is forced

307
00:19:25,330 --> 00:19:27,082
out of that woman's tongue.

308
00:19:27,791 --> 00:19:32,546
I promise you, this night
won't end without me finding out

309
00:19:32,629 --> 00:19:36,508
who is going to pay for
what happened to my grandson.

310
00:19:46,768 --> 00:19:48,312
[man] There's a 500,000 peso
reward for anybody

311
00:19:48,395 --> 00:19:50,397
who can provide information

312
00:19:50,647 --> 00:19:52,691
about what happened
during the mayor's shooting.

313
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:55,319
Who here knows about what happened?

314
00:19:57,905 --> 00:19:58,906
You.

315
00:20:00,574 --> 00:20:01,783
Do you know anything?

316
00:20:02,409 --> 00:20:04,244
[tense music playing]

317
00:20:10,459 --> 00:20:12,419
<i>Ivy, call us before the night is over.</i>

318
00:20:12,502 --> 00:20:13,795
<i>-If you don't</i>
<i>-All right, I will.</i>

319
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:15,297
<i>we'll attack the Ardientes ourselves.</i>

320
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:20,636
What time is it, Diego?
When are we leaving?

321
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:23,472
[Jepoy] I can't stay here!
What are we doing?

322
00:20:24,765 --> 00:20:25,891
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

323
00:20:26,391 --> 00:20:28,393
-Diego, are you going to find Lily?
-Yes, auntie.

324
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:29,895
-I'm coming with you.
-No, Auntie.

325
00:20:29,978 --> 00:20:32,147
Anna, stay here.
We won't take long. Let's go.

326
00:20:32,231 --> 00:20:33,565
Anna, stay here.

327
00:20:34,399 --> 00:20:37,110
[Camia] Guard, ready the car. Quickly.

328
00:20:40,739 --> 00:20:42,491
[suspenseful music playing]

329
00:20:53,168 --> 00:20:56,588
[tense music playing]

330
00:21:16,441 --> 00:21:17,901
[tense music swells]

331
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:31,623
[tense music continues]

332
00:21:52,269 --> 00:21:55,814
[grunting]

333
00:21:59,067 --> 00:22:01,236
[tense music playing]

334
00:22:27,596 --> 00:22:29,139
Diego, Jepoy.

335
00:22:29,222 --> 00:22:31,183
[breathing heavily]

336
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:33,894
Those damn Ardientes.

337
00:22:48,241 --> 00:22:49,159
Are you ready?

338
00:22:49,910 --> 00:22:50,911
Let's do this.

339
00:23:00,087 --> 00:23:01,630
[cell phone buzzing]

340
00:23:03,465 --> 00:23:04,716
[whispering] Wait, wait.

341
00:23:06,009 --> 00:23:07,052
[Diego] <i>Hello, who is this?</i>

342
00:23:07,344 --> 00:23:08,136
Diego?

343
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:09,554
Hello, Ivy? Where are you?

344
00:23:09,638 --> 00:23:10,472
Ivy?!

345
00:23:11,473 --> 00:23:12,390
Um…

346
00:23:12,724 --> 00:23:14,309
<i>Here. I'm with</i>

347
00:23:14,392 --> 00:23:15,352
the Ardientes.

348
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,063
Don't worry, I'm safe.

349
00:23:18,146 --> 00:23:21,024
We're at the hospital.
We'll save you from them.

350
00:23:23,026 --> 00:23:24,069
Don't.

351
00:23:24,152 --> 00:23:25,403
<i>Diego, don't.</i>

352
00:23:25,487 --> 00:23:26,446
Umm…

353
00:23:26,530 --> 00:23:31,743
I'm safe. I couldn't call right
away because I forgot my phone.

354
00:23:32,744 --> 00:23:34,079
<i>About Arnaldo…</i>

355
00:23:34,162 --> 00:23:37,165
Don't worry. He's in a coma.

356
00:23:37,249 --> 00:23:38,750
He can't rat me out.

357
00:23:39,334 --> 00:23:42,379
<i>Diego, please, don't do anything</i>
<i>that might get you killed.</i>

358
00:23:42,462 --> 00:23:43,922
Do you understand me?

359
00:23:44,005 --> 00:23:46,758
Don't do anything

360
00:23:46,842 --> 00:23:48,426
-that can get you--
-[phone beeps]

361
00:23:51,263 --> 00:23:53,181
Ivy? Ivy?!

362
00:23:54,432 --> 00:23:55,183
[sighs]

363
00:24:00,147 --> 00:24:01,189
Diego, they're leaving.

364
00:24:01,606 --> 00:24:02,357
Come on.

365
00:24:05,527 --> 00:24:07,028
[whispering] Jepoy, wait!

366
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:11,074
What are you doing, Diego?! Jepoy!

367
00:24:17,289 --> 00:24:18,540
[Jepoy] What?! Diego?

368
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:26,923
What's going on?

369
00:24:28,550 --> 00:24:29,926
Diego.

370
00:24:37,100 --> 00:24:38,268
[Jepoy] Diego!

371
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:43,481
Jepoy, Ivy called. She's safe. Let's go.

372
00:24:43,857 --> 00:24:44,900
-Let's go!
-Are you sure?

373
00:24:44,983 --> 00:24:45,901
Yes!

374
00:24:59,789 --> 00:25:01,124
-[Anna] Auntie?
-[Camia] Anna.

375
00:25:03,752 --> 00:25:05,462
[slow tense music playing]

376
00:25:08,215 --> 00:25:10,842
Arnaldo is like a ticking time bomb.

377
00:25:12,093 --> 00:25:15,055
Lily will be in grave danger
once he wakes up.

378
00:25:15,138 --> 00:25:17,057
[Camia] We must speed up our plans.

379
00:25:17,557 --> 00:25:21,102
[Anna] But Miss Cora is our
only witness against Emilia.

380
00:25:21,186 --> 00:25:23,021
[Anna] And we don't know where she is.

381
00:25:23,104 --> 00:25:26,274
But we know her address.
I'll sneak into her house

382
00:25:26,358 --> 00:25:30,153
in Sitio Nueve and look
for evidence against Emilia.

383
00:25:30,695 --> 00:25:31,821
Sitio Nueve?

384
00:25:32,322 --> 00:25:34,032
[Jepoy] Diego, the residents
there are pro-Ardiente.

385
00:25:34,574 --> 00:25:36,451
If they see you, they'll mob you.

386
00:25:36,701 --> 00:25:38,328
Why not ask someone else to do it?

387
00:25:38,745 --> 00:25:42,332
No. I won't involve others in this.

388
00:25:43,917 --> 00:25:45,168
I'll keep you guys posted.

389
00:25:45,710 --> 00:25:46,920
I'll help you.

390
00:25:47,462 --> 00:25:48,255
[Diego] No, Anna.

391
00:25:48,338 --> 00:25:49,673
It's too dangerous.

392
00:26:00,308 --> 00:26:01,851
[phone chimes]

393
00:26:03,228 --> 00:26:04,062
Boss?

394
00:26:04,145 --> 00:26:06,314
Tell all the guards to be on alert.

395
00:26:06,731 --> 00:26:08,566
Someone else is posing as the Jaguar.

396
00:26:08,900 --> 00:26:10,485
Yes, boss. Understood.

397
00:26:10,777 --> 00:26:12,362
[suspenseful music playing]

398
00:26:16,950 --> 00:26:19,369
[Raul] <i>I'm so close</i>
<i>to bringing Julio down.</i>

399
00:26:20,328 --> 00:26:22,330
<i>So I won't give you back your title.</i>

400
00:26:23,498 --> 00:26:24,416
<i>It's mine now.</i>

401
00:26:24,749 --> 00:26:28,461
<i>I am the real Jaguar.</i>
<i>And you're the impostor.</i>

402
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:31,506
[suspenseful music swells]

403
00:26:33,591 --> 00:26:36,594
[Mahjong tiles shuffling]

404
00:26:43,310 --> 00:26:44,853
[Raul's henchman 1] Good evening, boss.

405
00:27:01,161 --> 00:27:02,287
Boss, what brings you here?

406
00:27:02,370 --> 00:27:04,581
Our operations are running smoothly.

407
00:27:04,664 --> 00:27:06,333
-Is there a problem--
-[gunshot]

408
00:27:06,416 --> 00:27:08,293
[screaming]

409
00:27:09,044 --> 00:27:10,545
[Raul's henchman 3]
Boss?! Why did you do that?!

410
00:27:10,628 --> 00:27:12,714
[Raul's henchman 2 grunting]

411
00:27:15,383 --> 00:27:16,718
[Damian's henchman 1] Hands up!

412
00:27:17,510 --> 00:27:18,762
[Raul's henchman 3]
You aren't the real Jaguar!

413
00:27:19,304 --> 00:27:20,513
You're the impostor!

414
00:27:20,930 --> 00:27:21,931
[Raul's henchman 2 groaning]

415
00:27:22,015 --> 00:27:25,268
[Damian] Freaking morons!

416
00:27:26,853 --> 00:27:29,022
The man you call "boss"

417
00:27:30,732 --> 00:27:35,904
is the impostor. I am the real Jaguar!

418
00:27:36,905 --> 00:27:40,700
And starting today,
this gambling den is mine,

419
00:27:40,784 --> 00:27:43,328
and you'll work for me!

420
00:27:43,620 --> 00:27:48,625
Now, to those who refuse, raise your hand.

421
00:27:49,417 --> 00:27:50,293
Raise your--

422
00:27:51,002 --> 00:27:52,253
You refuse?

423
00:27:52,504 --> 00:27:54,130
-Don't!
-[gunshot]

424
00:27:55,590 --> 00:27:57,926
[laughs hysterically]

425
00:27:59,594 --> 00:28:01,054
He's dead!

426
00:28:08,186 --> 00:28:11,064
Where's Rufo? Why isn't he here?

427
00:28:11,689 --> 00:28:14,901
Boss Jaguar took care of him.
Because he betrayed us.

428
00:28:15,193 --> 00:28:16,319
What?

429
00:28:16,778 --> 00:28:20,573
Your fake boss is the real traitor here.

430
00:28:20,990 --> 00:28:24,369
[Damian] Tell him to give me back my men,

431
00:28:24,786 --> 00:28:29,165
my money, my weapons, women,

432
00:28:29,249 --> 00:28:30,959
and all the properties

433
00:28:31,042 --> 00:28:33,253
he acquired under the guise of Jaguar.

434
00:28:33,837 --> 00:28:35,338
Because if not,

435
00:28:35,964 --> 00:28:39,926
I will paint Poblacion Ardiente
red with his blood!

436
00:28:40,552 --> 00:28:42,887
Is that clear, morons?

437
00:28:45,849 --> 00:28:47,684
I can't hear you!

438
00:28:47,767 --> 00:28:48,935
[gunshot]

439
00:28:50,562 --> 00:28:53,106
-We'll tell him.
-Very good!

440
00:28:53,356 --> 00:28:59,738
[laughing hysterically]

441
00:29:34,063 --> 00:29:36,649
Jepoy, I think you should lie low for now.

442
00:29:37,442 --> 00:29:39,903
[Diego] Yes, Ivy can cover
for you from the Ardientes,

443
00:29:40,403 --> 00:29:42,363
but sooner or later,

444
00:29:42,697 --> 00:29:44,282
they'll find out that it was you
who shot Arnaldo.

445
00:29:44,365 --> 00:29:47,035
I don't care about the Ardientes, Diego!

446
00:29:47,118 --> 00:29:48,536
I won't run away from them.

447
00:29:49,120 --> 00:29:52,207
If I have to kill for Ivy, I'll do it.

448
00:29:52,415 --> 00:29:56,294
Jepoy, they'll stop at nothing
to take you out. You know them.

449
00:29:59,380 --> 00:30:00,715
Yes, I do.

450
00:30:02,884 --> 00:30:06,221
[tense music playing]

451
00:30:11,976 --> 00:30:12,936
[groans]

452
00:30:16,272 --> 00:30:18,066
[tense music continues]

453
00:30:19,150 --> 00:30:20,235
[phone clatters]

454
00:30:35,250 --> 00:30:36,334
Sit down!

455
00:30:37,126 --> 00:30:38,127
Sit down!

456
00:30:38,211 --> 00:30:39,838
I can sit myself down!

457
00:30:41,381 --> 00:30:42,507
[Jose] Tie her up.

458
00:30:44,259 --> 00:30:47,136
Oh, hello, Ardientes! You're back.

459
00:30:47,679 --> 00:30:49,180
Did you miss me already?

460
00:30:49,764 --> 00:30:52,892
Yada, yada, yada, yada, yada…

461
00:30:56,521 --> 00:30:57,605
Leave us.

462
00:30:58,398 --> 00:31:00,775
This is between me…

463
00:31:01,901 --> 00:31:02,944
and her.

464
00:31:04,612 --> 00:31:09,075
Go. Don't worry.
I can take care of myself.

465
00:31:16,666 --> 00:31:18,960
You have two options, Miss Aguas.

466
00:31:20,461 --> 00:31:22,130
Either you tell me the truth…

467
00:31:27,760 --> 00:31:30,805
[whirring]

468
00:31:33,224 --> 00:31:35,560
or watch me unleash hell.

469
00:31:37,979 --> 00:31:39,439
It's your choice.

470
00:31:41,190 --> 00:31:44,861
Do you remember what we did to Madrigal?

471
00:31:48,114 --> 00:31:50,658
You'll experience
something worse than that…

472
00:31:51,993 --> 00:31:55,538
if you do not tell me about
everything you did to Arnaldo.

473
00:31:56,623 --> 00:31:59,542
You really are getting old, Congressman.

474
00:31:59,626 --> 00:32:05,048
I told you, didn't I?
I did not shoot Arnaldo!

475
00:32:05,423 --> 00:32:09,010
[whirring]

476
00:32:14,807 --> 00:32:20,730
They say the eyes tell the truth

477
00:32:21,940 --> 00:32:24,442
and the mouth lies.

478
00:32:25,276 --> 00:32:27,737
I can see it in your eyes…

479
00:32:27,987 --> 00:32:30,615
all the horrible things
you did to my grandson!

480
00:32:34,077 --> 00:32:37,080
[drill whirring]

481
00:32:37,497 --> 00:32:41,376
[tense music playing]

482
00:32:43,962 --> 00:32:45,838
Go ahead! Kill me!

483
00:32:48,841 --> 00:32:50,134
Kill me.

484
00:32:50,593 --> 00:32:56,766
But if you do, Arnaldo
will go completely insane.

485
00:32:57,517 --> 00:33:00,478
If you kill Ivy Aguas,

486
00:33:00,561 --> 00:33:03,690
Mister Mayor will never get well.

487
00:33:05,066 --> 00:33:11,239
If you kill me, it'll be like
you killed your own grandson.

488
00:33:11,322 --> 00:33:15,076
Your only real grandson!

489
00:33:16,786 --> 00:33:19,330
[whirring]

490
00:33:22,583 --> 00:33:25,837
Go on! Do it!

491
00:33:27,046 --> 00:33:30,633
-I want the truth!
-You want the truth?!

492
00:33:32,301 --> 00:33:34,387
Why don't you have me take a paraffin test

493
00:33:34,470 --> 00:33:36,514
to get this over with?!

494
00:33:36,597 --> 00:33:40,852
Maybe that'll finally convince
you that I didn't shoot Arnaldo!

495
00:33:42,895 --> 00:33:44,272
You hear me?

496
00:33:44,772 --> 00:33:46,983
I hear you, silly girl.

497
00:33:48,609 --> 00:33:50,153
I'll give you one chance.

498
00:33:53,448 --> 00:33:55,783
I'll wait for you here, Congressman.

499
00:33:55,867 --> 00:33:58,953
But hurry. I can be really impatient.

500
00:33:59,370 --> 00:34:00,747
Silly girl.

501
00:34:00,830 --> 00:34:03,499
You're not going anywhere!
You're all tied up!

502
00:34:03,583 --> 00:34:07,920
For now. But I might surprise you.

503
00:34:11,549 --> 00:34:13,509
Go help old grandpa walk.

504
00:34:15,803 --> 00:34:19,807
[Julio chuckles] Nice try, little girl.

505
00:34:20,266 --> 00:34:22,185
I love you too!

506
00:34:26,189 --> 00:34:29,067
[tense music continues]

507
00:34:37,408 --> 00:34:38,951
[groaning]

508
00:34:41,287 --> 00:34:43,915
[grunting]

509
00:34:47,335 --> 00:34:49,712
[tense music continues]

510
00:34:56,385 --> 00:34:58,387
[grunting]

511
00:35:02,350 --> 00:35:05,103
[Ivy breathes heavily]

512
00:35:32,338 --> 00:35:34,048
[man] Congressman,

513
00:35:34,132 --> 00:35:36,676
we'll take these
to the crime lab for analysis.

514
00:35:36,759 --> 00:35:38,427
When will we get the results?

515
00:35:38,511 --> 00:35:39,679
[man] Tomorrow, Congressman.

516
00:35:39,762 --> 00:35:42,014
[Emilia] What? I can't wait
till tomorrow, Papa.

517
00:35:42,765 --> 00:35:44,475
Wait, let me handle it.
I'm going to do something

518
00:35:44,559 --> 00:35:47,937
for us to know
the truth this very evening.

519
00:35:48,020 --> 00:35:49,730
[tense music plays]

520
00:35:49,814 --> 00:35:51,482
What do you have in mind?

521
00:35:53,609 --> 00:35:55,736
Let me handle it, Papa.

522
00:35:56,362 --> 00:35:59,991
[tense music swells]

523
00:36:09,292 --> 00:36:11,377
Listen up, Ivy Aguas…

524
00:36:12,211 --> 00:36:14,755
I'm sure you've known all
this time how much I hate you.

525
00:36:14,839 --> 00:36:16,841
But the thing is, you're so good

526
00:36:16,924 --> 00:36:18,509
at bluffing and telling lies.

527
00:36:18,593 --> 00:36:20,261
You've actually mastered them.

528
00:36:20,344 --> 00:36:22,972
So, I'll have you undergo
a lie detector test

529
00:36:23,055 --> 00:36:25,141
to reveal the truth.

530
00:36:25,224 --> 00:36:29,478
You can never be too careful.
Dishonesty is contagious.

531
00:36:29,562 --> 00:36:32,690
And I'm really scared
that I'll catch your disease.

532
00:36:32,773 --> 00:36:34,400
It's fatal.

533
00:36:34,483 --> 00:36:36,861
Well, I guess what they say is true.

534
00:36:36,944 --> 00:36:39,947
Paranoia is contagious.

535
00:36:40,907 --> 00:36:42,992
But I understand, Emilia.

536
00:36:43,075 --> 00:36:44,827
And I feel bad for you.

537
00:36:44,911 --> 00:36:47,371
Because after all the crimes
you've committed,

538
00:36:47,455 --> 00:36:50,625
you think everyone else is out to get you.

539
00:36:50,708 --> 00:36:54,670
Excuse me? You know, believe it or not,

540
00:36:54,754 --> 00:36:59,133
you're the only one on this
whole planet I'm suspicious of.

541
00:36:59,217 --> 00:37:00,551
[Emilia] Just you.

542
00:37:00,635 --> 00:37:04,805
Too bad you're just insecure
because you see me as a threat.

543
00:37:04,889 --> 00:37:06,766
[chuckles]

544
00:37:06,849 --> 00:37:09,560
[Emilia] Is that how highly
you think of yourself?

545
00:37:09,644 --> 00:37:13,648
Me? Insecure of you? Wrong.

546
00:37:13,731 --> 00:37:16,234
Excuse me, I still wear the crown.

547
00:37:16,317 --> 00:37:17,193
Then keep it.

548
00:37:17,276 --> 00:37:19,695
-But I have the throne.
-Fine.

549
00:37:19,779 --> 00:37:22,865
Let's see where that arrogance
takes you after we reveal

550
00:37:22,949 --> 00:37:26,494
all the dirty secrets
you've been keeping from us.

551
00:37:27,245 --> 00:37:29,413
I'm not keeping any secrets.

552
00:37:29,497 --> 00:37:30,957
Well then, good.

553
00:37:31,707 --> 00:37:33,084
[snaps fingers] Shall we start?

554
00:37:34,585 --> 00:37:39,298
[suspenseful music playing]

555
00:37:46,347 --> 00:37:49,558
Okay. First question.

556
00:37:50,893 --> 00:37:53,437
Is your name Ivy Aguas?

557
00:37:57,733 --> 00:37:58,985
Yes.

558
00:37:59,944 --> 00:38:02,738
Okay. Second question.

559
00:38:04,448 --> 00:38:07,285
Do you have plans
to bring down the Ardientes?

560
00:38:08,911 --> 00:38:10,955
What kind of question is that?
Of course, not--

561
00:38:11,038 --> 00:38:12,957
-Just answer it!
-I don't!

562
00:38:16,544 --> 00:38:17,920
Third question.

563
00:38:18,921 --> 00:38:22,508
Are you Diego Torillo
and Camia Cruz's spy?

564
00:38:27,680 --> 00:38:28,681
Never.

565
00:38:28,764 --> 00:38:30,433
Hmm…

566
00:38:30,808 --> 00:38:33,561
Okay. Next question will be…

567
00:38:34,020 --> 00:38:37,523
Are you the one
who planned Arnaldo's downfall?

568
00:38:40,735 --> 00:38:43,654
I would never do that to him.

569
00:38:44,363 --> 00:38:46,365
Were you the one who shot Arnaldo?

570
00:38:46,449 --> 00:38:47,408
No!

571
00:38:47,491 --> 00:38:50,995
But you know who shot my son! Yes or no?!

572
00:38:53,581 --> 00:38:55,249
Answer my question!

573
00:38:56,959 --> 00:38:59,253
[Julio] One wrong answer…

574
00:39:02,548 --> 00:39:04,300
and you're dead.

575
00:39:07,595 --> 00:39:09,680
Do I have to keep repeating myself?

576
00:39:10,389 --> 00:39:11,265
I already told you

577
00:39:11,349 --> 00:39:15,519
that I didn't see the face
of the man who shot Arnaldo!

578
00:39:23,986 --> 00:39:26,238
Come on. Tell me she's lying.

579
00:39:28,616 --> 00:39:31,452
Her heart rate and blood
pressure are normal.

580
00:39:31,535 --> 00:39:33,162
She's telling the truth.

581
00:39:33,746 --> 00:39:35,748
[laughs]

582
00:39:37,124 --> 00:39:38,626
[Ivy] See?

583
00:39:39,668 --> 00:39:40,878
Okay?

584
00:39:41,796 --> 00:39:44,673
So, Emilia?
Do you have any more questions?

585
00:39:44,757 --> 00:39:46,175
Go ahead and ask them.

586
00:39:46,258 --> 00:39:48,636
Otherwise, you're just wasting our time.

587
00:39:50,596 --> 00:39:52,223
One last question.

588
00:39:53,808 --> 00:39:54,809
Are you ready?

589
00:39:55,267 --> 00:39:57,061
[tense music plays]

590
00:39:59,271 --> 00:40:01,774
Are you Lily Cruz?

591
00:40:14,161 --> 00:40:15,663
[tense music swells]

592
00:40:15,746 --> 00:40:17,790
Are you Lily Cruz?!

593
00:40:19,959 --> 00:40:22,044
Emilia, what does that have to do with--

594
00:40:22,128 --> 00:40:23,879
Just answer the damn question!

595
00:40:23,963 --> 00:40:25,673
Are you Lily Cruz?!

596
00:40:25,756 --> 00:40:27,633
I am not Lily Cruz!

597
00:40:30,511 --> 00:40:32,179
Tell me. Tell me she's lying!

598
00:40:32,263 --> 00:40:35,641
-She's telling the truth.
-Oh, come on!

599
00:40:36,350 --> 00:40:38,602
Check the machine! Maybe it's defective!

600
00:40:38,686 --> 00:40:41,063
Have them check your head too!

601
00:40:41,147 --> 00:40:44,567
That's what's defective!
Not their machine.

602
00:40:45,693 --> 00:40:48,571
Even if the results of that
damn machine don't change,

603
00:40:48,654 --> 00:40:51,198
you can never change what I think of you!

604
00:40:51,657 --> 00:40:57,163
You can lie straight to my face,
but you can never ever fool me!

605
00:40:59,915 --> 00:41:01,083
Are you done?

606
00:41:07,006 --> 00:41:09,717
Emilia, since you've asked
all of your questions…

607
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:11,677
Now, it's my turn.

608
00:41:12,470 --> 00:41:15,514
You see, liars supposedly
hate other liars too.

609
00:41:15,598 --> 00:41:20,769
Why don't you sit here
and take the lie detector test?

610
00:41:20,853 --> 00:41:25,900
Because maybe you're
the one keeping secrets…

611
00:41:26,942 --> 00:41:27,943
from your family.

612
00:41:28,652 --> 00:41:29,945
Let's find out the truth!

613
00:41:30,029 --> 00:41:34,241
So we'll know who the real liar
is between us.

614
00:41:34,658 --> 00:41:36,160
Okay, what's the result?

615
00:41:36,243 --> 00:41:40,289
Come on! Give it to me now!
I want to hear it!

616
00:41:40,372 --> 00:41:41,123
Again?

617
00:41:41,207 --> 00:41:44,293
He already gave you the results!
You're stupid and deaf.

618
00:41:44,376 --> 00:41:47,546
What?! It's still the same?!

619
00:41:47,922 --> 00:41:49,423
[tense music playing]

620
00:41:49,507 --> 00:41:50,508
[shouts]

621
00:41:58,557 --> 00:42:01,227
[Ivy] <i>You think you can</i>
<i>outsmart me, Emilia?</i>

622
00:42:01,310 --> 00:42:04,480
<i>Sorry to say, but I'm smarter than you.</i>

623
00:42:04,563 --> 00:42:07,274
<i>I'll do whatever it takes</i>
<i>to make my plans succeed.</i>

624
00:42:07,358 --> 00:42:11,737
<i>Don't ever try to challenge me, Emilia,</i>

625
00:42:11,820 --> 00:42:14,365
<i>because I'll never let you catch me alive.</i>

626
00:42:17,284 --> 00:42:19,286
[suspenseful music playing]

627
00:42:25,084 --> 00:42:25,960
Well?

628
00:42:26,043 --> 00:42:28,170
Aren't you going to do or say something?!

629
00:42:28,629 --> 00:42:30,256
Why? What do you want me to do?

630
00:42:30,339 --> 00:42:32,132
Oh, come on. I can't believe this, Raul!

631
00:42:32,216 --> 00:42:35,970
You don't want to make Ivy pay
for what she did to Arnaldo?!

632
00:42:36,053 --> 00:42:37,388
Why would I do that?

633
00:42:37,471 --> 00:42:39,598
She proved her innocence, didn't she?

634
00:42:39,682 --> 00:42:41,100
And you believed that?!

635
00:42:41,600 --> 00:42:44,687
I don't believe things
that easily, Emilia.

636
00:42:44,770 --> 00:42:48,857
I need to know the truth first
before I make a move.

637
00:42:48,941 --> 00:42:51,110
-That is so weak!
-Watch what you say.

638
00:42:51,193 --> 00:42:52,319
You're crossing the line!

639
00:42:52,903 --> 00:42:56,824
Well, Raul, if you won't do
anything about it, then, I will!

640
00:42:56,907 --> 00:42:59,952
I'll talk to someone
and that's the Jaguar!

641
00:43:00,035 --> 00:43:02,621
Don't do that, Emilia.
You don't know that bastard.

642
00:43:07,668 --> 00:43:08,669
Emilia!

643
00:43:15,509 --> 00:43:17,511
[ominous music playing]

644
00:43:20,931 --> 00:43:24,351
Your paraffin test came back.

645
00:43:25,603 --> 00:43:26,854
It was negative.

646
00:43:28,772 --> 00:43:29,982
I'm not surprised.

647
00:43:30,065 --> 00:43:31,567
[Julio scoffs]

648
00:43:31,817 --> 00:43:35,195
Don't celebrate just yet, Miss Aguas.

649
00:43:37,281 --> 00:43:39,908
You may have passed all the tests…

650
00:43:41,493 --> 00:43:43,954
but that doesn't mean you're off the hook.

651
00:43:46,165 --> 00:43:52,254
It may be true that
you didn't shoot Arnaldo.

652
00:43:54,673 --> 00:44:00,429
And it might be true
you didn't see the face

653
00:44:01,096 --> 00:44:03,974
of the person who did that to Arnaldo.

654
00:44:05,809 --> 00:44:07,728
But that doesn't mean…

655
00:44:09,396 --> 00:44:11,607
you didn't want to have him killed.

656
00:44:20,157 --> 00:44:23,202
You better be careful, Ivy.

657
00:44:25,037 --> 00:44:28,207
Don't let me catch you

658
00:44:29,875 --> 00:44:35,089
because my bullet
is faster than your karma.

659
00:44:40,052 --> 00:44:42,763
If I wanted to kill Arnaldo,

660
00:44:44,390 --> 00:44:47,017
I would've done that a long time ago.

661
00:44:49,061 --> 00:44:50,979
So, next time, Congressman,

662
00:44:51,063 --> 00:44:54,900
think twice before making
false accusations against me,

663
00:44:54,983 --> 00:44:58,445
because you don't know
what I'm capable of!

664
00:44:59,655 --> 00:45:01,115
[suspenseful music playing]

665
00:45:01,198 --> 00:45:04,118
Watch your words, Miss Aguas!

666
00:45:05,619 --> 00:45:10,374
Because this knife's sharper
than your tongue.

667
00:45:16,755 --> 00:45:18,757
[tense music swells]

668
00:45:23,303 --> 00:45:27,516
[somber piano music playing]

669
00:45:31,979 --> 00:45:36,900
[Ivy] <i>It doesn't matter if</i>
<i>I suffer or get tortured.</i>

670
00:45:37,526 --> 00:45:42,823
<i>I can take the pain if it means</i>
<i>I can protect my loved ones.</i>

671
00:45:42,906 --> 00:45:45,159
<i>Please spare them.</i>

672
00:45:47,244 --> 00:45:50,581
[dramatic music playing]

673
00:46:09,808 --> 00:46:11,268
[Jose] Congressman.

674
00:46:11,351 --> 00:46:12,561
Yes?

675
00:46:12,644 --> 00:46:14,188
Someone wants to talk to you.

676
00:46:14,897 --> 00:46:16,190
Who is it?

677
00:46:20,694 --> 00:46:23,197
Tell the Congressman everything you know.

678
00:46:24,198 --> 00:46:27,534
I'm Chito, the caretaker
of one of the yachts

679
00:46:27,618 --> 00:46:29,745
docked near the site
where the mayor was shot.

680
00:46:30,704 --> 00:46:32,372
I came to you first.

681
00:46:32,456 --> 00:46:34,541
I haven't gone to the police yet.

682
00:46:36,126 --> 00:46:38,795
What do you know about what happened?

683
00:46:42,549 --> 00:46:43,383
[gunshot]

684
00:46:44,676 --> 00:46:48,180
[Chito] <i>I heard several gunshots</i>
<i>that night.</i>

685
00:46:48,722 --> 00:46:50,891
[Diego] <i>Come on, Jepoy. The lights are on.</i>

686
00:46:51,934 --> 00:46:54,478
[Diego] <i>I hope they're here.</i>
<i>Hurry, come on!</i>

687
00:46:54,770 --> 00:46:57,898
[tense music playing]

688
00:47:00,817 --> 00:47:02,819
[gunshots]

689
00:47:04,780 --> 00:47:08,450
[Chito] <i>After that, I saw two</i>
<i>men fleeing the crime scene.</i>

690
00:47:23,757 --> 00:47:26,176
I'll never forget their faces.

691
00:47:28,345 --> 00:47:31,557
Congressman, we asked an artist
to make a cartographic sketch

692
00:47:31,640 --> 00:47:33,767
based on the witness' description.

693
00:47:33,850 --> 00:47:37,437
[suspenseful music playing]

694
00:47:41,108 --> 00:47:42,734
[Jose] It's Diego Torillo

695
00:47:42,818 --> 00:47:44,945
and your former employee, Madrigal.

696
00:47:49,533 --> 00:47:52,244
[suspenseful music swells]

697
00:47:53,370 --> 00:47:56,081
[Julio] <i>One million for Madrigal's body.</i>

698
00:47:56,164 --> 00:47:59,543
<i>And another million for Diego's corpse.</i>

699
00:47:59,626 --> 00:48:01,628
[Cora] <i>My conscience keeps eating at me.</i>

700
00:48:01,712 --> 00:48:04,339
<i>I'm ready to divulge</i>
<i>Mrs. Emilia's corrupt activities.</i>

701
00:48:04,423 --> 00:48:07,718
[Julio] <i>I will go against Diego Torillo.</i>

702
00:48:07,801 --> 00:48:10,012
<i>I will run for governor.</i>

703
00:48:10,095 --> 00:48:13,724
[Ivy] <i>This election's going to be</i>
<i>dirtier and bloodier.</i>

704
00:48:13,807 --> 00:48:15,809
<i>Jepoy and Diego's lives are in danger.</i>

705
00:48:15,892 --> 00:48:17,394
<i>Julio has issued a shoot-to-kill order</i>

706
00:48:17,477 --> 00:48:18,520
-<i>against them.</i>
-[gunshots]

707
00:48:18,604 --> 00:48:19,730
-[women screaming]
-[gunshots]

708
00:48:19,813 --> 00:48:21,189
-<i>Get down!</i>
-[gunshots]

709
00:48:21,273 --> 00:48:22,149
[people screaming]

710
00:48:22,232 --> 00:48:23,775
[Camia] <i>What's happening?!</i>

711
00:48:24,526 --> 00:48:25,777
<i>Mom!</i>

712
00:48:25,861 --> 00:48:27,779
[theme music playing]
